{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Mobile Price: the struck price, and the white band under checkout.

  ---------------------------------------------------- 1. THE STRUCK PRICE

  A cart line is a CSS grid with named areas. The price lives in `pr` and the
  quantity stepper in `qt`, immediately to its left.

  The price element is .nc-lsave -- nc-linesave's, NOT the theme's p.price,
  which is hidden on any line carrying a saving. Its base rule is a flex ROW
  with white-space:nowrap, so the struck compare-at and the price charged sit
  side by side and refuse to wrap. When that pair is wider than the column it
  overflows LEFT, into `qt`, and the old price runs under the + button. A
  struck number beside a quantity reads as a struck quantity.

  NO MEDIA QUERY -- and this is the correction that mattered. The first pass
  scoped this to max-width:600px, reasoning about phones. But the constraint
  here is the width of the DRAWER, not the width of the screen: the cart panel
  is roughly 380-420px whatever it is opened on, so the same overflow happens
  on a desktop browser, where a 600px query never fires. The rule now applies
  wherever the cart is.

  Stacking turns the overflow into height, which the row has to spare, and
  order:-1 lifts the struck figure ABOVE the price charged, so it reads
  was-then-now down the column. Both .nc-lsave and p.price are covered, since
  which renders depends on whether the line has a saving, and the struck figure
  is matched as <s>, <del> or by strike-through class, because which of those
  the cart emits varies by line type.

  ---------------------------------------------------- 2. THE WHITE BAND

  The band under CHECKOUT is the sticky footer's own doing. position:sticky
  with bottom:0 pins to the bottom of the VIEWPORT only while its container is
  taller than the screen; on a short cart the element sits at its natural place
  in the flow and the container's remaining height stays blank below it.
  Padding was never the cause, which is why trimming padding never moved it.

  That one IS phone-scoped: the sticky footer is only set below 600px in
  pg-cart-fast, so there is nothing to undo above it.

  Ordered after pg-cart-fast in footer-group, so it overrides that file's
  sticky rule at equal specificity.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* ---- struck price above the price charged, at every width ---- */
  #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave,
  #cart .l4ca > li section .nc-lsave,
  #cart .l4ca > li .price,
  #cart .l4ca > li section .cols p.price{
    display:flex !important;
    flex-direction:column !important;
    align-items:flex-end !important;
    justify-content:flex-end !important;
    flex-wrap:nowrap !important;
    gap:1px !important;
    line-height:1.15 !important;
    text-align:right !important;
    max-width:100% !important;
    overflow:visible !important;
  }
  #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave s,
  #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave del,
  #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave [class*="old"],
  #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave [class*="was"],
  #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave [class*="compare"],
  #cart .l4ca > li .price s,
  #cart .l4ca > li .price del{
    order:-1 !important;
    display:block !important;
    width:auto !important;
    margin:0 !important;
    font-size:12px !important;
    font-weight:600 !important;
    line-height:1.15 !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
  }

  /* ---- no white band under the button ---- */
  @media (max-width: 600px){
    #cart .sticky-in-panel{
      position:static !important;
      bottom:auto !important;
      padding-bottom:calc(4px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) !important;
      margin-bottom:0 !important;
    }
  }
</style>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Mobile Price", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
